{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects","id":1224076,"title":"The Sea of Oblivion, and What It Reflects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-01T21:24:11-07:00","id":1224076,"title":"The Sea of Oblivion, and What It Reflects","content":"Oblivion is an infinite sea of black water at the bottom of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The tombs of the never born stand above it on stone pillars. Every year those pillars lower by an inch. Every year, those waters recede by an inch.<br /> <br /> It is known that, in the underworld, Mount Meru is a great wound in the world, a staircase spiraling down towards that infinite sea. The sea that all things flow towards, which gives nothing back that falls into it, hidden from the world and underworld alike by a great and forbidding labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Those ghosts of the dead that lay eyes upon the waters of oblivion often slip into those waters and vanish forever, leaving no trace. Only the living can look upon the waters of oblivion without feeling a call to fall in to them.<br /> <br /> Within those black waters, there are 150 lights shining beneath the surface: the solar shards, broken from the jade prison, that were sacrificed to Oblivion, and as they were sacrificed and slept beneath those black waters, their dark reflections rose to take their place.<br /> <br /> The abyssal exaltations are dark mirrors to the solar exaltation. They are gifts from Oblivion. The price that was paid for them still remains within oblivion, in the dark waters, for any foolish enough to retrieve it.<br /> <br /> The abyssal exalted are the eyes and ears of oblivion. It\u2019s sees through them. It knows the world through them. It hungers through them.<br /> <br /> Those who sold their death to oblivion in exchange for Exaltation will never know peace from it. Always the void sees through them, and when it sees life, the black waters stir with hunger, and grow turbulent.<br /> <br /> The secret of the abyssal exalted is this: their exultation bears no great curse because it was created long after the curse was laid down. No solar shard beats with in their heart. Something stranger, from a sea that has never known the sun, rides within them.<br /> <br /> What you must know of the primordial ones is this: we invented death and mortality and age and sickness to free ourselves from them, and only those who never knew the rule of the primordial ones question the wisdom of this choice.<br /> <br /> Only outside the garden of Eden could we find a weapon that could kill them, and we left without regrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T13:40:45-07:00","id":1224222,"title":"","content":"That's not my preferred vision for Oblivion, but is it polite for me to share my dissenting viewpoint in this thread? I don't want to be rude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:27:08-07:00","id":1224570,"title":"","content":"Having intentionally steered away from any descriptions of the Underworld (mechanical and lyrical) to prevent spillage of player knowledge into my character knowledge I don't feel bound to not comment. <br /> <br /> In the absence of a canonical knowledge base to contradict this viewpoint I must say I find it very evocative and poetic. Like looking through a dark mirror to the distorted reflection beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:56:40-07:00","id":1224691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KFinigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224570#post1224570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the absence of a canonical knowledge base to contradict this viewpoint I must say I find it very evocative and poetic. Like looking through a dark mirror to the distorted reflection beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But is it gameable?<br /> <br /> (More importantly, how do you see any reflection when you look <i>through</i> a mirror into what is <i>beyond </i>it? Maybe it's a one-way mirror and the room on the other side has a different mirror on the wall?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T22:21:18-07:00","id":1224896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224691#post1224691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But is it gameable?<br /> <br /> (More importantly, how do you see any reflection when you look <i>through</i> a mirror into what is <i>beyond </i>it? Maybe it's a one-way mirror and the room on the other side has a different mirror on the wall?)</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd part first, i take the line of looking through the dark mirror to the reflection beyond as not taking it as a reflection, but instead considering the image on the other side of it like another world. If my reflection in some weird mirror makes me look freaky, what would life be like always looking that way? That kind of feeling is what it sounds like to me.<br /> <br /> As for whether the idea is gameable, i feel like it is and takes away some assumptions of prior underworld models. First is Abyssal interactions with 'redemption'. If they don't actually host the shards, then they can't directly change with them. Instead they would have to go down into the depths and recover the solar shard, possibly ruining their own source of power in the process before saving it.<br /> <br /> The rest of it is a nice description that makes me think of using the Neverborn more like the Yozis in the idea of Landscapes/people. Neverborn are as close to Oblivion as they can be, so their environmental bodies try to reflect Oblivion. What is the crushing waves and waters, another may be the endless labyrinth we are used to getting. Mixing up our views of something like Oblivion while keeping the ever crushing theme of it makes me feel more inspired about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T02:04:08-07:00","id":1224917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224896#post1224896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd part first, i take the line of looking through the dark mirror to the reflection beyond as not taking it as a reflection, but instead considering the image on the other side of it like another world. If my reflection in some weird mirror makes me look freaky, what would life be like always looking that way? That kind of feeling is what it sounds like to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, it sounds more like somebody really wanted to sound poetic and, in the process, kinda... forgot that a metaphor doesn't just have to sound cool, it also has to <i>make sense</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224896#post1224896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for whether the idea is gameable, i feel like it is and takes away some assumptions of prior underworld models. First is Abyssal interactions with 'redemption'. If they don't actually host the shards, then they can't directly change with them. Instead they would have to go down into the depths and recover the solar shard, possibly ruining their own source of power in the process before saving it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting ideas - I'm genuinely glad that you're getting use out of it!<br /> <br /> However, I specifically take issue with this part:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects#post1224076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The abyssal exalted are the eyes and ears of oblivion. It\u2019s sees through them. It knows the world through them. It hungers through them.<br /> <br /> Those who sold their death to oblivion in exchange for Exaltation will never know peace from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems very rooted in Goodwinian thought, and sounds both utterly impractical to implement and tediously unfun to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T05:51:25-07:00","id":1224935,"title":"","content":"To me, Oblivion is best as a state of being. Or rather, non-being.<br /> <br /> When a spirit is permanently destroyed, it has been Obliviated.<br /> <br /> When a human\u2019s higher soul enters Lethe, their identity is Obliviated.<br /> <br /> When a higher soul is permanently destroyed, the soul itself is Obliviated.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn desperately seek Obliviation to free them from the pain of undeath.<br /> <br /> The Well of Oblivion could be a hole that stretches down infinitely or actually lead to a point where anything entering it becomes Obliviated. No one knows, and if it isn\u2019t, then the hole becomes a metaphor for the futility of the Neverborn\u2019s efforts. <br /> <br /> Deathlords would derive no power from Oblivion any more than someone could draw power from Elsewhere; their power comes from the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal Exalted draw power from their own Exaltations, which draw power from nothing, but have been twisted to reflect the Neverborn and the Deathlords, and thus the nature of the Underworld and ghosts.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is not a force. It is not a creature with any will or desire. It is just the state of \u201cnot-existing\u201d. Total destruction. Annihilation.<br /> <br /> That is true \u201cnothingness\u201d. \u201cNothing\u201d has no power or motives. It is nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T10:06:17-07:00","id":1224996,"title":"","content":"I liked it. I don't know that I'd use it, but I liked reading it and it does have some interesting points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:49:03-07:00","id":1225668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224917#post1224917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, it sounds more like somebody really wanted to sound poetic and, in the process, kinda... forgot that a metaphor doesn't just have to sound cool, it also has to <i>make sense</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was half-asleep when I wrote the first draft of this, up too late and dictating it to Siri, so it's definitely a bit rambly. But it's not meant to be a metaphor - you literally go down to the bottom of the world and see the endless black waters of Oblivion there. In retrospect, it's at least partly inspired by Ash Lake from the first Dark Souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1224917#post1224917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems very rooted in Goodwinian thought, and sounds both utterly impractical to implement and tediously unfun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's unambiguously rooted in Goodwinian interpretations of Resonance. I've always found Abyssals most interesting as fundamentally irredeemable - like entropy itself, their sin cannot be defeated, but it can be kept almost eternally at bay with mindful coping mechanisms. I'm uninterested in Oblivion reaching out and spontaneously making the Abyssal's life horrible - but I like the idea that, at some level, they can never be free of the end of all things. They are a gift, or a curse, brought back from beyond the end of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:56:59-07:00","id":1225673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1225668#post1225668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was half-asleep when I wrote the first draft of this, up too late and dictating it to Siri, so it's definitely a bit rambly. But it's not meant to be a metaphor - you literally go down to the bottom of the world and see the endless black waters of Oblivion there. In retrospect, it's at least partly inspired by Ash Lake from the first Dark Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...But that part... wasn't about your writing...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224076-the-sea-of-oblivion-and-what-it-reflects?p=1225668#post1225668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's unambiguously rooted in Goodwinian interpretations of Resonance. I've always found Abyssals most interesting as fundamentally irredeemable - like entropy itself, their sin cannot be defeated, but it can be kept almost eternally at bay with mindful coping mechanisms. I'm uninterested in Oblivion reaching out and spontaneously making the Abyssal's life horrible - but I like the idea that, at some level, they can never be free of the end of all things. They are a gift, or a curse, brought back from beyond the end of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a fascinating conversation to be had here about Abyssals, playerbase expectations, purity of design versus playability, and a host of other related topics, buuuuut I kinda have an exam tomorrow. I'll get back to you about the subject when I'm able, if that's okay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}